␀read_rollback␀write_rollback␀read_lock_status␀write_lock_status␀part_size␀part_guid␀read␀perm_attr_test␀verify␀boot_android␀Execute the Android Bootloader flow.␀<interface> <dev[:part|;part_name]> <slot> [<kernel_addr>]
    - Load the Boot Control Block (BCB) from the partition 'part' on
      device type 'interface' instance 'dev' to determine the boot
      mode, and load and execute the appropriate kernel.
      In normal and recovery mode, the kernel will be loaded from
      the corresponding "boot" partition. In bootloader mode, the
      command defined in the "fastbootcmd" variable will be
      executed.
      On Android devices with multiple slots, the pass 'slot' is
      used to load the appropriate kernel. The standard slot names
      are 'a' and 'b'.
    - If 'part_name' is passed, preceded with a ; instead of :, the
      partition name whose label is 'part_name' will be looked up in
      the partition table. This is commonly the "misc" partition.
␀android_print_hdr␀print android image header␀<partition name>␀boot_fit␀Boot FIT Image from memory or boot/recovery partition␀boot_fit [addr]␀bootz␀boot Linux zImage image from memory␀booti␀boot arm64 Linux Image image from memory␀coninfo␀print console devices and information␀crypto_sum␀crypto checksum engine␀[md5|sha1|sha256|sha512] [addr] [length]␀dtimg␀manipulate dtb/dtbo Android image␀dump <addr>
    - parse specified image and print its structure info
      <addr>: image address in RAM, in hex
dtimg start <addr> <index> <varname>
    - get address (hex) of FDT in the image, by index
      <addr>: image address in RAM, in hex
      <index>: index of desired FDT in the image
      <varname>: name of variable where to store address of FDT
dtimg size <addr> <index> <varname>
    - get size (hex, bytes) of FDT in the image, by index
      <addr>: image address in RAM, in hex
      <index>: index of desired FDT in the image
      <varname>: name of variable where to store size of FDT␀echo␀echo args to console␀[args..]
    - echo args to console; \c suppresses newline␀exit␀exit script␀ext4load␀load binary file from a Ext4 filesystem␀<interface> [<dev[:part]> [addr [filename [bytes [pos]]]]]
    - load binary file 'filename' from 'dev' on 'interface'
